{
  "reason": "Commands whose replies hand out something with a remote lifetime: contexts, user contexts, preload scripts, intercepts, data collectors, subscriptions, screencasts and extensions. A reply that arrives after its caller was interrupted, or timed out, is routed to an owner, which adopts or releases it (PROTOCOL.md, Protocol client). `release` names the spec's own counterpart command. Remote objects a script.callFunction or script.evaluate hands out are released by L1, which knows their target, with script.disown.",
